From: alikhanyessaly <alikhan.yessaly@quantum.edu.kz>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 08:30:56 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] btstack: system services and stack kept up for bleterm

- ATT read/write callbacks dispatch the bleterm system block first and
  tolerate missing user state (NULL root pointers).
- register_service_begin(false) re-adds the fixed system block (GAP, GATT
  Service Changed indicate, NUS, PBL) while bleterm runs.
- mp_bluetooth_init split into stack_up() (no GC objects) and
  user_state_create(); while bleterm runs, deinit only tears down user
  state (pending notify ops unlinked, ATT DB reset to the system block).
- gap_advertise(None) restores bleterm's advertising payload.
- mp_bluetooth_is_active() also requires user state.
